      "writtenOn": "2023-12-05T16:53:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMO, this would be more straightforward by building on the [comment I had](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/2792452/comment/9b6f4a79_87193154/) on aosp/2792452 and making `locate_overlay_target_path` return an `Option` i.e.\n```\nlet Some(node_path) \u003d vm_dtbo.locate_overlay_target_path(dtbo_node_path)? else {\n    continue;\n}; \nif let Some(node) \u003d fdt.node(\u0026node_path)? {\n    let info \u003d AssignedDeviceInfo::parse(node, node_path, dtbo_node_path, hyp)?;\n    assigned_devices.push(info);\n} else {\n    filtered_dtbo_paths.push(dtbo_node_path.into());\n}\n```\ninstead of introducing a new error whose only purpose is to be caught. Yes, we\u0027re passing `node` and `node_path` (ownership transfer!) so it\u0027s the responsibility of the caller to ensure that they match but the whole flow is more straightforward and easier to maintain and reason about.",
